WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.767
It was near Greece

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.501
had a dangerously

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.936
overloaded boat crowded with.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:06.272
More than 750 migrants capsized in June.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.675
Almost everyone on board drowned,

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:09.843
including a 14 year

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.244
old boy from Pakistan.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.712
Women and children were locked

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:13.847
in the boat's cargo hold,

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:14.381
according to U.N.

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:15.015
officials,

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:17.050
and had little chance for survival.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.284
CNN traveled to his home

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:19.052
in Punjab Province

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.421
and spoke to his devastated father.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.055
CNN's Anna

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:25.125
Coren has this exclusive report.

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:27.927
From the lush plains of Gujarat

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.396
in Punjab Province

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:29.929
are home to

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.398
some of the most fertile land

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.900
in all of Pakistan.

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:35.301
The mighty Indus River

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.404
and its tributaries, the lifeblood.

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.206
But not everyone here

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:43.443
prospers from its richness.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:44.144
14 year

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:44.844
old Muhammad

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.246
Abuza felt the heavy

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.214
burden of responsibility.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.082
His father,

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.583
a school van driver earning

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:51.885
less than $90

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.453
a month, was struggling to

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:54.654
provide for the family

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:57.023
Abu abuser,

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:57.924
worried about the

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.893
future of his younger brothers,

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:02.028
especially six year old Hasan,

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.663
who is severely disabled.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.031
We have about him in the article.

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:05.698
Leave it up.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.967
My son pleaded with me to be sent abroad,

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.302
he explains.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:09.636
He said,

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:11.738
Look at how we live will die of hunger.

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.373
It's best for me to leave.

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:15.208
So I can support our family

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.776
very hard here.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.545
Many older boys from the village

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:20.480
had already made the trek to Europe

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.682
through human smuggling operations,

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:25.051
sending hefty remittances back home

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:26.619
and are not doing them on either

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:27.787
one of these abusers.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.923
Uncle had decided to go.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:31.124
And the teenager knew

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:34.127
this was his chance.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:36.396
The people smuggler said it would cost

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.298
more than 8,000 USD

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.999
to send my son to Italy.

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.835
I said I can't afford it.

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:42.435
He told me,

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.603
Your kid will earn that

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:44.904
in a couple of months.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:48.541
At the beginning of May this year, Abuza,

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:49.342
his uncle

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:51.111
and a small group of teenage boys

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:54.280
from the village set off human smugglers

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.381
organize for the group

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.784
to fly from Karachi to Dubai,

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.453
then to Egypt, before transiting to Libya

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.856
from Tripoli International Airport.

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:04.357
They drove to the Libyan port

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:05.658
city of Tobruk

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:06.960
and waited in a camp

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.828
filled with other illegal migrants

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:10.930
for the next month.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.099
The day before the group

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:14.367
set sail for Italy,

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.136
their final destination.

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:16.669
Abu Zar

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:18.638
sent a video to his brothers,

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.673
hoping to make them laugh.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:22.175
He then recorded the group's

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:25.311
final prayers on a car

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:27.280
that night.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.415
He called his father,

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:30.850
Ari Gold Body.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.652
My son was really happy.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:33.987
He said, Don't worry, Dad.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.321
It will be okay.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:36.389
We'll have lifejackets.

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:37.590
It's a big boat.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.358
Once on there,

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:40.260
you'll have nothing to worry about.

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:43.763
On the 9th of June, Mabuza

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:45.465
boarded the Adriana,

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:48.401
a fishing vessel with a capacity of 100

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:49.802
instead.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.839
750 illegal migrants were crammed

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:55.008
aboard, of which almost half

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.209
were from Pakistan.

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:57.544
According to the Pakistani

00:02:57.544 --> 00:02:59.512
Interior Ministry,

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:00.380
within days,

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:00.947
the trawler

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:03.183
would capsize off the coast of Greece

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.785
as a Greek coastguard ship watched on

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:09.722
more than 600 people drowned in

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:10.657
what would become

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:11.791
one of the deadliest

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.460
migrant boat tragedies.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.931
Among the survivors, only 12 Pakistanis

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.466
abuser was not one of them.

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:22.569
You must see the whole country

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:24.604
dying of hunger is better than this.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:27.307
Don't send your children away for us.

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:28.341
Life in hell

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:30.443
are now the same water today.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.546
But this grieving father's warning

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.748
is falling on deaf ears.

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:37.684
According to UN migration

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.285
last year, Pakistanis weren't

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:41.454
even among the top ten nationalities

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.156
arriving in Europe.

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:44.290
This year, however,

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.025
they're ranked number five,

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.527
with economic migration

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:49.362
fueling the surge.

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.130
A financial crisis in Pakistan

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.132
and record high unemployment

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.467
is driving many families

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.603
to make this life altering decision.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:57.937
Common narrative

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.572
that smugglers are there

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:00.106
to sort of

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:01.174
lure people

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:03.376
into into this dangerous journey.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:04.577
We look at

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:05.979
who are the people that influence

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:07.480
the decision of migrating

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.048
and is mostly family.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:11.784
So migration is a family investment.

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:13.920
For this mother

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:14.821
in Bengali

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.889
in Pakistan administered Kashmir.

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:17.890
Her 20 year

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.726
old son was supposed to be on

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:21.661
that ill fated vessel.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.263
She says the human traffickers

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.531
disembarked him because of overcrowding.

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:28.268
He's now waiting for the next boat.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.570
Like right now, just him to come home.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:31.404
But he won't.

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:32.639
She explains

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:33.906
he wants to go to Europe

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.808
like other boys from our village.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:38.911
I pray that he makes it

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.247
Anna Coren, CNN, Hong Kong.

